  "page1": {
    "title": "Adding Fractions Fairly",
    "subtitle": "Two slices of pizza, two bottoms — make them match first.",
    "body": "Mia eats half of a pizza. Her brother eats one fourth of it. How much do they eat in all?\n\nWe want to add 1/2 and 1/4. But the bottom numbers are not the same. The bottom number is the <u>denominator</u>. We cannot add until the bottoms match.\n\nSo we change 1/2 into 2/4, and now both bottoms are 4. This step is called finding a common bottom. The two pieces are now the same size.\n\nNow we add the tops. We <mark>add the top numbers</mark> only. So 2/4 plus 1/4 is 3/4. The bottom number stays 4.\n\nMia and her brother eat 3/4 of the pizza, and adding is fair when the bottoms match!",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/03.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Two pizza slices, 2/4 and 1/4, joining to make 3/4 of a whole pizza."
  },
